{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116366",
      "title": "Introducing HTTP Interceptors",
      "lectureOrder": 238,
      "videoOrder": 227,
      "sourceHash": "a1e3b2fd667045de37be4a59889caa80d98669509601b371e729881e85a73ed0",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 2.34,
          "en": "Now, last but not least,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.34,
          "end": 4.17,
          "en": "to conclude this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.17,
          "end": 7.23,
          "en": "there's one last HTTP client feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.23,
          "end": 9.03,
          "en": "I also want to cover here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.03,
          "end": 12.3,
          "en": "even though we don't need it in this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.3,
          "end": 16.23,
          "en": "Because Angular's HTTP client actually allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.23,
          "end": 19.89,
          "en": "to register so-called interceptors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.89,
          "end": 23.1,
          "en": "which are special functions that will be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.1,
          "end": 25.5,
          "en": "when a request is about to be sent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.5,
          "end": 27.84,
          "en": "or when a response arrived.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.84,
          "end": 32.22,
          "en": "So that besides the place where you triggered a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.22,
          "end": 36.18,
          "en": "or where you subscribed to the request observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.18,
          "end": 37.38,
          "en": "besides these places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.38,
          "end": 40.2,
          "en": "you've got another place where you can execute logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.2,
          "end": 42.6,
          "en": "That's the idea behind interceptors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.6,
          "end": 45.09,
          "en": "Now, to register such an interceptor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.09,
          "end": 46.53,
          "en": "you should go to the place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.53,
          "end": 49.563,
          "en": "where you provide the HTTP client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.7,
          "end": 54.99,
          "en": "And to this function you can actually pass another function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.99,
          "end": 58.77,
          "en": "or the result of calling another function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.77,
          "end": 63.603,
          "en": "the result of calling the withInterceptors function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.37,
          "end": 68.01,
          "en": "And withInterceptors is also imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.01,
          "end": 70.203,
          "en": "from Angular common HTTP.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.94,
          "end": 74.31,
          "en": "WithInterceptors then takes an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.31,
          "end": 78.53999999999999,
          "en": "And here you now register all the interceptor functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.53999999999999,
          "end": 81.24,
          "en": "that should be executed by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.24,
          "end": 85.5,
          "en": "for any outgoing request or incoming response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.5,
          "end": 89.88,
          "en": "Now, such an interceptor function is just a regular function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.88,
          "end": 92.4,
          "en": "and you could store it in any file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.4,
          "end": 94.71000000000001,
          "en": "Here, I'll just store it in the main.ts file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.71000000000001,
          "end": 98.37,
          "en": "so that we see it side by side with this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.37,
          "end": 100.53,
          "en": "but you could store it anywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.53,
          "end": 102.33,
          "en": "And I'll name it loggingInterceptor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.41,
          "end": 105.663,
          "en": "But the name, as so often, is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.62,
          "end": 110.793,
          "en": "It's worth noting though that it's a function, not a class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.75,
          "end": 115.53,
          "en": "In the past, in older Angular versions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.53,
          "end": 119.31,
          "en": "you would actually create interceptors as classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.31,
          "end": 120.9,
          "en": "And you'll find more information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.9,
          "end": 122.76,
          "en": "about that in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.76,
          "end": 124.77,
          "en": "But the more modern and recommended way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.77,
          "end": 127.203,
          "en": "is to create them as functions instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.46,
          "end": 130.59,
          "en": "Now, such an interceptor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 130.59,
          "end": 132.573,
          "en": "then accepts two arguments:",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.41,
          "end": 136.466,
          "en": "the intercepted request object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.466,
          "end": 140.34,
          "en": "and next function, as it turns out to be,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.34,
          "end": 144.51,
          "en": "which you would call to allow the intercepted requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.51,
          "end": 147.123,
          "en": "to continue, but you'll see it in action soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.17000000000002,
          "end": 150.72,
          "en": "Now, it's a good idea to add type annotations here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 150.72,
          "end": 155.55,
          "en": "to tell TypeScript the value types of these parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.55,
          "end": 158.34300000000002,
          "en": "And for the request, the type is HttpRequest,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 159.99,
          "end": 163.59300000000002,
          "en": "which is a type imported from Angular common HTTP.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.06,
          "end": 170.06,
          "en": "And for next, it's HttpHandlerFn, for handler function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.68,
          "end": 176.013,
          "en": "which is also imported from Angular common HTTP.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.02,
          "end": 180.81,
          "en": "HttpRequest is actually a generic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 180.81,
          "end": 184.02,
          "en": "which needs extra type information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 184.02,
          "end": 187.74,
          "en": "Specifically here you can pass unknown as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 187.74,
          "end": 191.43,
          "en": "to make it clear that this could be any kind of request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 191.43,
          "end": 194.04,
          "en": "transporting any kind of value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 194.04,
          "end": 197.613,
          "en": "So this here in the end defines the request body type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 199.07999999999998,
          "end": 200.67000000000002,
          "en": "Now with that we have a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 200.67000000000002,
          "end": 202.89,
          "en": "that could be used as an interceptor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.89,
          "end": 204.27,
          "en": "but it's not doing anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 204.27,
          "end": 207.723,
          "en": "and it would currently actually break any requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 208.82999999999998,
          "end": 210.12,
          "en": "So what you should do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210.12,
          "end": 214.29,
          "en": "to allow intercepted requests to eventually continue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 214.29,
          "end": 218.32,
          "en": "is you should call this next parameter as a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 219.81,
          "end": 223.203,
          "en": "and pass the intercepted request to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 225.27,
          "end": 227.25,
          "en": "With that, the interceptor in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 227.25,
          "end": 229.32,
          "en": "wouldn't have any effect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 229.32,
          "end": 234.21,
          "en": "So to see an effect, I'll log Outgoing Request here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 234.21,
          "end": 239.16,
          "en": "for example, and then log the request object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 239.16,
          "end": 241.86,
          "en": "so that we can see which kind of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 241.86,
          "end": 244.443,
          "en": "we would have access to in this interceptor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 246,
          "end": 250.02,
          "en": "And then I'll also pass this logging interceptor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 250.02,
          "end": 253.103,
          "en": "as a value to this interceptor's array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 254.16,
          "end": 256.32,
          "en": "Important you don't execute it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 256.32,
          "end": 259.983,
          "en": "you just pass it as a function to withInterceptors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 263.25,
          "end": 265.8,
          "en": "With that, if you go back and you open your terminal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 265.8,
          "end": 269.43,
          "en": "and you reload, you'll see Outgoing Request twice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 269.43,
          "end": 272.79,
          "en": "because we are sending two requests initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 272.79,
          "end": 274.71,
          "en": "one for the available places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 274.71,
          "end": 276.633,
          "en": "and one for the favorite places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 277.74,
          "end": 279.84000000000003,
          "en": "We can see the request objects here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 279.84000000000003,
          "end": 284.25,
          "en": "and see the data that we could access in the interceptor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 284.25,
          "end": 287.34000000000003,
          "en": "We see the headers that have been added automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 287.34000000000003,
          "end": 290.90999999999997,
          "en": "We can see the request method here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 290.90999999999997,
          "end": 293.79,
          "en": "the request body, if there would be any,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 293.79,
          "end": 297.543,
          "en": "the URL to which it's sent, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 298.92,
          "end": 300.66,
          "en": "Now, you're of course not limited",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 300.66,
          "end": 302.823,
          "en": "to just outputting information here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 303.69,
          "end": 306.63,
          "en": "Instead, you can actually produce a new request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 306.63,
          "end": 311.34,
          "en": "by calling the clone method on the existing request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 311.34,
          "end": 314.88,
          "en": "because you can't mutate the original request directly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 314.88,
          "end": 317.403,
          "en": "but you can clone it to produce a new one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 318.39,
          "end": 321.69,
          "en": "And to clone, you can pass an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 321.69,
          "end": 325.863,
          "en": "which defines which parts of the requests should be changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 326.97,
          "end": 330.723,
          "en": "For example, you could change the body or the headers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 331.8,
          "end": 335.04,
          "en": "And here I'll change my headers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 335.04,
          "end": 338.523,
          "en": "to use the original request headers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 339.36,
          "end": 342.03,
          "en": "and call set to add a new header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 342.03,
          "end": 343.8,
          "en": "So that will give us all the old headers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 343.8,
          "end": 345.573,
          "en": "plus one new header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 346.8,
          "end": 347.76,
          "en": "And here for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 347.76,
          "end": 352.263,
          "en": "we could set the X-DEBUG header to TESTING,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 354.03,
          "end": 357.15,
          "en": "which won't do anything but which we should be able to see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 357.15,
          "end": 358.803,
          "en": "in the developer tools later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 359.79,
          "end": 363.06,
          "en": "And it would then be that cloned and updated request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 363.06,
          "end": 364.683,
          "en": "that should be forwarded here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 367.26,
          "end": 369.51,
          "en": "With that, if you save that and you go back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 369.51,
          "end": 371.46,
          "en": "you'll be greeted by some errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 371.46,
          "end": 373.71,
          "en": "because actually with that new header added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 373.71,
          "end": 376.113,
          "en": "the backend doesn't allow access anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 377.31,
          "end": 380.31,
          "en": "For the moment, that's not too important here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 380.31,
          "end": 383.2,
          "en": "Instead now here we can go to the network tab",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 384.81,
          "end": 387.81,
          "en": "and reload and find those failing requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 387.81,
          "end": 391.08,
          "en": "And they are under headers, under Request Headers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 391.08,
          "end": 394.413,
          "en": "You should see that header at the very bottom.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 396.9,
          "end": 399.27,
          "en": "Now again here, it won't do anything helpful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 399.27,
          "end": 401.43,
          "en": "Indeed, it will break the application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 401.43,
          "end": 404.90999999999997,
          "en": "but that is how you could manipulate a request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 404.90999999999997,
          "end": 406.77,
          "en": "and for example, change its headers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 406.77,
          "end": 408.93,
          "en": "which could be one thing you might wanna do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 408.93,
          "end": 411.15,
          "en": "with such an interceptor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 411.15,
          "end": 413.04,
          "en": "so that you add some special header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 413.04,
          "end": 415.14300000000003,
          "en": "to all your outgoing requests.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
